CueLight's models were trained on, and build on, the third-party work below. Each is used under its own license.
Where weights or data were changed (fine-tuned, re-segmented, relabeled or used for training), that's noted.

Model weights

- CueLight-Base is fine-tuned from the encoder of OpenAI's Whisper small.en
  (https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-small.en), released under the Apache License 2.0. The encoder was modified
  (made causal) and fine-tuned. Whisper's code is Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI, under the MIT License
  (LICENSES/whisper-MIT.txt).
- Whisper base.en and medium.en (OpenAI, Apache-2.0 weights and MIT code) were used as teachers during training.
- Smart Turn v3.2 (https://github.com/pipecat-ai/smart-turn), Copyright (c) 2024-2025, Daily, under the BSD 2-Clause
  License (LICENSES/smart-turn-BSD-2-Clause.txt). No Smart Turn code is included here.

Training data (Creative Commons Attribution, used for training after re-segmenting and relabeling)

- Smart Turn v3.2 training data, pipecat-ai/smart-turn-data-v3.2-train, CC BY 4.0, by Pipecat / Daily, with audio
  contributed by Liva AI, Midcentury and MundoAI.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/pipecat-ai/smart-turn-data-v3.2-train
- The People's Speech (clean and dirty subsets), MLCommons, CC BY. Galvez et al., "The People's Speech: A Large-Scale
  Diverse English Speech Recognition Dataset for Commercial Usage", 2021.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/MLCommons/peoples_speech
- Harper Valley Bank, Gridspace and Stanford University, CC BY 4.0.
  https://github.com/cricketclub/gridspace-stanford-harper-valley
- Open Yap 1K sample, The Agentic Data Company, CC BY 4.0.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/TheAgenticDataCompany/open-yap-1k
- eot-bench data, LiveKit, CC BY 4.0, used to choose between models and for evaluation.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/livekit/eot-bench-data

Conditions passed on from the data: please don't use CueLight, or audio processed with it, to identify speakers or to
clone voices.

